    "feminine": "Still here. \"Two.\" Still here. The water holds her the way water does — steady and quiet — and {{CHILD_NAME}} floats, and counts, and Khaled counts alongside, and the numbers fill up the space where the fear was. Not all of it. But enough. \"Three. Four. Five.\""
  },
  {
    "pageNumber": 12,
    "masculine": "His feet find the floor again. {{CHILD_NAME}} stands up. Water streams down his face and he blinks and looks back — at the rope with the red and white floats, at the shallow end, bright and busy on the other side. And then he looks down at where his feet are standing right now. Which is past the rope. Not far past it. But past.",
